rker of liver injury caused by drug toxicity, infection, alcohol, and steatosis. A related gene on chromosome 16 encodes a putative mitochondrial alanine aminotransaminase.[provided by RefSeq, Nov 2009].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P24298","text":"Pyridoxal enzyme tha catalyzes the reversible transamination between alanine and 2-oxoglutarate to form pyruvate and glutamate (PubMed:11863375). By mediating the conversion of these four major intermediate metabolites, plays an important role in gluconeogenesis and amino acid metabolism (PubMed:11863375)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}